        title: "Background",
        html: "<p>Dr. Lindsay McKittrick grew up in Kansas and completed medical school at the University of Kansas Medical Center. She moved to Utah to complete her pediatric residency training at Primary Children’s Hospital and joined our Salt Lake office in 2025.</p>\n<p>As a pediatrician, Dr. McKittrick is passionate about implementing healthy habits and improving mental health for children, teens, and their families. She enjoys helping families learn and finds it rewarding to partner with them through the ups and downs of childhood and parenthood. Her approach to pediatrics centers around a “child-first” mindset, striving to provide the best treatment for each child – both in the present moment and with their future in mind. As a result, Dr. McKittrick has a strong focus on preventive medicine and supporting development.</p>\n<p>Outside the office, Dr. McKittrick loves camping, hiking, and skiing with her husband and friends. She enjoys crafting, reading, and gardening – even if her green thumb isn’t quite as strong as her pediatric skills!  Dr. McKittrick is available for a friendly ‘Meet &amp; Greet’ and is eager to care for your family over the years to come.</p>",
